1
00:00:00,288 --> 00:00:02,805
So we have different kinds of instructions,

2
00:00:03,254 --> 00:00:05,499
system instructions built into the agent,

3
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:08,016
and then maybe our custom instructions in an

4
00:00:08,594 --> 00:00:09,524
agent.md file.

5
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:13,548
What about skills and memory then? Agent

6
00:00:13,644 --> 00:00:14,270
skills

7
00:00:14,927 --> 00:00:18,006
is a standardized way to give AI agents new

8
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:20,154
capabilities and expertise. That's not

9
00:00:20,154 --> 00:00:21,549
something I made up or

10
00:00:22,078 --> 00:00:24,211
the Anthropic team invented for Claude

11
00:00:24,323 --> 00:00:27,065
Cowork or Claude Code. Instead, it's a

12
00:00:27,065 --> 00:00:29,905
standard. Which is implemented by many

13
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:32,747
agents, many agentic pieces of software,

14
00:00:33,212 --> 00:00:35,829
like that AgentsMD approach, but

15
00:00:36,423 --> 00:00:39,297
unlike AgentsMD for not loading instructions

16
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:42,733
in general into every context window, into

17
00:00:42,862 --> 00:00:43,632
every new session,

18
00:00:44,226 --> 00:00:47,421
but instead on demand when a certain task

19
00:00:47,502 --> 00:00:50,263
would benefit from that skill. Now that may

20
00:00:50,263 --> 00:00:52,559
still sound quite abstract, so let's zoom in

21
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:55,851
a bit. An agent skill. As standardized and

22
00:00:56,172 --> 00:00:58,371
as supported by many agents out there,

23
00:00:58,917 --> 00:01:00,908
is in the end just a folder so that it can

24
00:01:00,989 --> 00:01:03,461
also be easily shared between projects. You

25
00:01:03,477 --> 00:01:05,645
can just put it into a project you plan to

26
00:01:05,645 --> 00:01:06,721
work on with an agent.

27
00:01:07,668 --> 00:01:11,377
And then in that skill folder, you have a

28
00:01:11,377 --> 00:01:14,797
skill.md file and it must be named skill.md,

29
00:01:15,118 --> 00:01:18,073
which also like agents.md includes some

30
00:01:18,105 --> 00:01:20,529
special instructions or extra pieces of

31
00:01:20,593 --> 00:01:22,649
knowledge you want the agent to have.

32
00:01:23,643 --> 00:01:24,717
Then you can also have some

33
00:01:25,406 --> 00:01:28,451
extra resources combined with SkillMD, like

34
00:01:28,451 --> 00:01:31,448
certain scripts or deep dive resources or

35
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:34,061
assets like templates, for example, but

36
00:01:34,061 --> 00:01:34,958
we'll get back to that.

37
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:37,651
The SkillMD file is the important one. And

38
00:01:37,651 --> 00:01:40,231
to make this less abstract, in that demo

39
00:01:40,312 --> 00:01:41,642
folder, which I provided to you,

40
00:01:42,299 --> 00:01:45,424
you will find 2 folders,.agents and

41
00:01:45,585 --> 00:01:47,219
.clawed. If you can't see them, you must

42
00:01:47,284 --> 00:01:49,255
make sure that your Finder or Windows

43
00:01:49,303 --> 00:01:52,076
Explorer shows hidden folders and files. And

44
00:01:52,172 --> 00:01:54,291
just as with AgentsMD and ClaudeMD,

45
00:01:54,965 --> 00:01:57,261
.claude is for Claude Cowork and Claude

46
00:01:57,309 --> 00:01:57,646
Code,

47
00:01:58,176 --> 00:02:00,728
.agents is for most other agents. Both

48
00:02:01,065 --> 00:02:04,308
folders, as you can see, simply contain a

49
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:05,175
skills folder.

50
00:02:05,977 --> 00:02:07,679
If we open that skills folder,

51
00:02:08,225 --> 00:02:09,830
in this case, in this demo project I

52
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,687
provided to you, you'll see 3 subfolders.

53
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:16,347
And it's one subfolder per agent skill

54
00:02:16,957 --> 00:02:19,766
as standardized that you want to provide to

55
00:02:19,782 --> 00:02:22,768
your AI agent for a certain project. For

56
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:24,872
example, a data analytics skill.

57
00:02:25,578 --> 00:02:28,757
If I open that skill with a text editor

58
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:31,326
again, this skill.md file, you'll see that

59
00:02:31,326 --> 00:02:33,493
in there, there is this weird part at the

60
00:02:33,493 --> 00:02:35,901
top. That's some metadata separated from the

61
00:02:35,901 --> 00:02:38,952
main content by being put in such a block

62
00:02:39,128 --> 00:02:41,280
starting and ending with 3 dashes. We'll get

63
00:02:41,296 --> 00:02:41,842
back to that.

64
00:02:42,484 --> 00:02:44,057
But then it's the main content of the skill,

65
00:02:44,266 --> 00:02:46,626
the piece of information or instructions you

66
00:02:46,754 --> 00:02:49,322
want to expose to an AI agent. Now, as I

67
00:02:49,322 --> 00:02:51,646
mentioned earlier, the difference compared

68
00:02:51,646 --> 00:02:54,113
to AgentsMD is that these files should be

69
00:02:54,113 --> 00:02:57,254
loaded on demand by the agent when it's

70
00:02:57,318 --> 00:02:58,616
working on a certain task.

71
00:02:59,337 --> 00:03:02,590
Whereas AgentsMD and ClaudeMD are always

72
00:03:02,686 --> 00:03:04,962
injected into the context window, so are

73
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:06,917
always part of a conversation,

74
00:03:07,510 --> 00:03:09,401
no matter what the agent is working on.

75
00:03:10,138 --> 00:03:12,253
So for example, the data analytics skill

76
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,432
should of course only be activated and

77
00:03:14,544 --> 00:03:15,618
loaded and This

78
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:18,476
text here should only be injected into the

79
00:03:18,476 --> 00:03:20,836
context window if the agent is really

80
00:03:20,965 --> 00:03:23,052
working on a data analytics task.

81
00:03:23,614 --> 00:03:24,962
Otherwise, it should not be loaded.

82
00:03:26,118 --> 00:03:28,558
And then this skill actually also has some

83
00:03:29,169 --> 00:03:31,962
extra nested folder, the references folder

84
00:03:32,283 --> 00:03:33,503
with another document.

85
00:03:34,386 --> 00:03:37,485
Because one core concept behind agent skills

86
00:03:37,822 --> 00:03:40,937
is progressive disclosure, which means these

87
00:03:40,985 --> 00:03:41,498
skills

88
00:03:42,157 --> 00:03:43,779
are not loaded upfront,

89
00:03:44,341 --> 00:03:47,522
but instead discovered and activated on

90
00:03:47,618 --> 00:03:47,923
demand.

91
00:03:48,582 --> 00:03:51,087
Upfront, only the skill's name and

92
00:03:51,087 --> 00:03:53,015
description is loaded into the context

93
00:03:53,015 --> 00:03:53,320
window.

94
00:03:54,139 --> 00:03:56,822
And that's this metadata part. So only this,

95
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:00,773
the name and description of all the skills,

96
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:03,343
all 3 skills in my case here, are loaded

97
00:04:03,696 --> 00:04:06,877
like the entire content of AgentsMD upfront

98
00:04:06,989 --> 00:04:09,639
into the context window of every new agent

99
00:04:09,639 --> 00:04:11,853
session. But only that, not the main

100
00:04:11,869 --> 00:04:15,189
content. This saves token and also makes

101
00:04:15,189 --> 00:04:17,354
sure that the agent doesn't have any

102
00:04:17,354 --> 00:04:20,128
instructions or notes in its context window

103
00:04:20,465 --> 00:04:22,084
that don't really matter to it yet.

104
00:04:22,774 --> 00:04:24,746
Now, this description should then give the

105
00:04:24,859 --> 00:04:27,472
agent a hint regarding when that skill

106
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,451
should be activated.

107
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:31,305
So in this case here, I have a pretty clear

108
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:33,710
hint that this skill should be used when

109
00:04:33,919 --> 00:04:36,469
answering business or data questions and so

110
00:04:36,501 --> 00:04:40,043
on. Now, many agents or agentic pieces of

111
00:04:40,043 --> 00:04:42,672
software, many harnesses, I should say, like

112
00:04:42,753 --> 00:04:47,129
Claude Cowork have built-in logic to detect

113
00:04:47,401 --> 00:04:50,351
those skills if they are stored in the right

114
00:04:50,367 --> 00:04:53,621
path. So in a.claudskills folder, for

115
00:04:53,637 --> 00:04:55,561
example, in case of Claude Cowork.

116
00:04:56,202 --> 00:04:58,158
And then you must have one folder per skill

117
00:04:58,222 --> 00:05:00,225
and you must have a skill.md file. And if

118
00:05:00,225 --> 00:05:01,828
you follow that convention, it will be

119
00:05:01,828 --> 00:05:03,816
discovered by Claude Cowork, but they will

120
00:05:03,976 --> 00:05:06,044
only register this description and they have

121
00:05:06,221 --> 00:05:09,058
internal logic so that they expose this

122
00:05:09,202 --> 00:05:12,409
skill almost like a tool to the AI agent.

123
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,456
And just like for a tool, the AI agent can

124
00:05:15,456 --> 00:05:18,631
make a request to load or to activate, you

125
00:05:18,647 --> 00:05:21,276
could say, a skill. So to read the rest of

126
00:05:21,292 --> 00:05:21,950
the context.

127
00:05:22,992 --> 00:05:25,269
And only when that decision was made by the

128
00:05:25,381 --> 00:05:26,471
agent, only then

129
00:05:27,081 --> 00:05:29,357
is the entire skill MD file read. And then

130
00:05:29,566 --> 00:05:31,650
the instructions can be followed or the

131
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:33,751
extra information can be used. But even

132
00:05:33,799 --> 00:05:35,466
then, the agent can dive deeper. For

133
00:05:35,482 --> 00:05:38,033
example, in this skill, I refer to some

134
00:05:38,209 --> 00:05:40,520
other Markdown file in a subfolder, in the

135
00:05:40,536 --> 00:05:43,039
references subfolder, and that was not

136
00:05:43,039 --> 00:05:45,687
loaded automatically. Instead, since the

137
00:05:45,687 --> 00:05:48,511
agent now, once it loaded skill-md, is aware

138
00:05:48,559 --> 00:05:51,062
of that subfolder and the file in there, it

139
00:05:51,062 --> 00:05:54,159
can again request to read that file.

140
00:05:54,913 --> 00:05:56,967
And that's how an agent, how a large

141
00:05:56,999 --> 00:05:59,951
language model can progressively discover

142
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:02,952
skills and related files through that

143
00:06:02,952 --> 00:06:04,845
officially standardized mechanism.

144
00:06:05,904 --> 00:06:09,291
But again, just as with AgentsMD, if your

145
00:06:09,355 --> 00:06:12,838
agent you built doesn't have a mechanism for

146
00:06:12,950 --> 00:06:15,695
discovering those SkillMD files and doesn't

147
00:06:15,695 --> 00:06:17,027
support that standard,

148
00:06:18,006 --> 00:06:20,173
the feature is not there. Just because it's

149
00:06:20,173 --> 00:06:22,372
a standard does not mean that your software,

150
00:06:22,677 --> 00:06:24,892
your agent you might have built, supports

151
00:06:24,924 --> 00:06:27,235
it. You may be building some task-specific

152
00:06:27,235 --> 00:06:29,466
agent that doesn't need to dynamically

153
00:06:29,498 --> 00:06:32,387
discover more information or skills because

154
00:06:32,387 --> 00:06:35,098
it is very focused on one main task and

155
00:06:35,098 --> 00:06:37,567
doesn't need extra pieces of dynamically

156
00:06:37,583 --> 00:06:40,630
loaded information. It is up to you, the

157
00:06:40,726 --> 00:06:43,901
person building an agent, whether you want

158
00:06:43,917 --> 00:06:46,658
to support features like AgentsMD or this

159
00:06:46,722 --> 00:06:48,181
agent skills standard.

160
00:06:48,823 --> 00:06:50,939
But of course, pretty much all of the more

161
00:06:50,971 --> 00:06:53,809
generic general agents like Claude Cowork,

162
00:06:54,114 --> 00:06:57,465
but also ChatGPT and so on, do support that

163
00:06:57,465 --> 00:06:58,363
skills feature.

164
00:06:59,084 --> 00:07:01,730
And in Claude Cowork, for example, you can,

165
00:07:01,794 --> 00:07:02,163
for one,

166
00:07:03,174 --> 00:07:04,667
Go to the skill setting

167
00:07:05,904 --> 00:07:06,176
and then

168
00:07:06,931 --> 00:07:08,087
add new skills here.

169
00:07:08,954 --> 00:07:11,700
But if you loaded a folder, it will also

170
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:14,060
discover skills in that folder automatically

171
00:07:14,317 --> 00:07:16,485
when working in that folder. So for example,

172
00:07:16,501 --> 00:07:18,556
here where I loaded this Claude data

173
00:07:18,572 --> 00:07:21,687
analysis folder, which has the skills loaded

174
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:21,928
or

175
00:07:22,506 --> 00:07:22,747
in it,

176
00:07:23,405 --> 00:07:27,130
if I ask analyze the sales CSV file,

177
00:07:28,126 --> 00:07:29,552
it will go ahead

178
00:07:30,226 --> 00:07:33,656
and it will find my data analytics skill and

179
00:07:33,816 --> 00:07:36,429
most likely also activate it. We can also

180
00:07:36,477 --> 00:07:38,609
see that here it read some memory and I'll

181
00:07:38,786 --> 00:07:41,142
get back to memory later. We can also see

182
00:07:41,206 --> 00:07:43,418
that it listed files on the computer. So

183
00:07:43,451 --> 00:07:44,989
it's taking a look at the files it has

184
00:07:45,118 --> 00:07:47,250
access to, but that really is just that one

185
00:07:47,378 --> 00:07:49,831
folder it has access to here. And you see it

186
00:07:50,007 --> 00:07:52,844
also read a skill.md file and those general

187
00:07:52,844 --> 00:07:54,543
instructions I mentioned earlier. And then

188
00:07:54,912 --> 00:07:57,301
another skill as well, probably because it

189
00:07:57,381 --> 00:07:59,641
also plans on creating a report and the

190
00:07:59,641 --> 00:08:01,744
server is busy, what can you do? But that's

191
00:08:02,033 --> 00:08:04,329
the idea behind agent skills. And that's

192
00:08:04,458 --> 00:08:07,156
another important, very common way of

193
00:08:07,589 --> 00:08:11,170
loading more context into the agent session.

194
00:08:11,588 --> 00:08:14,302
But again, it depends on how the agent or

195
00:08:14,735 --> 00:08:16,871
the agentic piece of software was built.

196
00:08:17,449 --> 00:08:19,858
And of course, if you as the user then want

197
00:08:19,858 --> 00:08:21,994
to use that feature. If you are not

198
00:08:22,042 --> 00:08:24,836
providing any skills, there of course aren't

199
00:08:24,852 --> 00:08:26,683
any for the agent to load.
